[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"520","stub":{"id":"520","section":"Swamp Creek Trail to White Sand Creek","altname":"","river":"Big Sand Creek","difficulty":"V","states":["USA-IDA"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"109774","location":{"latitude":"46.3899993896484","longitude":"-114.583602905273"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"115026","location":{"latitude":"46.4123992919922","longitude":"-114.527603149414"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"4","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"18813","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4243","description":"","caption":"The incomparable Big Sands \"shuttle\"","poi_name":"Blowdown Gnar","subject":"Sweaty boaters","author":"Jesse Kodadek","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18813","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18813"}},{"id":"18817","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4243","description":"Seems like an easy hike in at this point.","caption":"Big Sands hike looking good to start","poi_name":"The nice, friendly part of the trail","subject":"Etzel, Colorado Chris, Hoheim","author":"Jesse Kodadek","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18817","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18817"}},{"id":"18801","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4243","description":"","caption":"Biggest hole of the day","poi_name":"","subject":"Ira Vasgaard","author":"Jesse Kodadek","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18801","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18801"}},{"id":"18809","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4243","description":"","caption":"First big rapid","poi_name":"First big class V drop","subject":"Ira","author":"Jesse Kodadek","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18809","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18809"}},{"id":"18803","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4243","description":"First drop of long, technical rapid that featured multiple freakish holes.","caption":"First drop of one of the stout crux rapids","poi_name":"","subject":"Ira","author":"Jesse Kodadek","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18803","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18803"}},{"id":"18807","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4243","description":"Stouter than it looks","caption":"Finishing the first large class V rapid","poi_name":"After the waterfall","subject":"Ira","author":"Jesse Kodadek","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18807","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18807"}},{"id":"18811","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4243","description":"After a 3 mile hike in, the put in gives no indication of the gradient you are about to encounter.","caption":"Put in for Big Sands","poi_name":"The only placid spot","subject":"Kevin, James, Ira - UNCA reunion","author":"Jesse Kodadek","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18811","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18811"}},{"id":"18818","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4243","description":"Seems like an easy hike in at this point.","caption":"Big Sands hike looking good to start","poi_name":"The nice, friendly part of the trail","subject":"Etzel, Colorado Chris, Hoheim","author":"Jesse Kodadek","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18818","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18818"}},{"id":"18805","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4243","description":"No one tangled with this bad boy. Long, complex, technical, pushy, and with a sieve ending. ","caption":"Everyone portaged this one","poi_name":"","subject":"The world famous Kevin Colburn","author":"Jesse Kodadek","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18805","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18805"}}],"detail":{"id":"520","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Big Sands Creek is a full day mission for most mortals that dishes out long, high quality Class IV and V rapids in a beautiful canyon.\n\nThe trip begins with a fairly long (45 minutes+) drive from highway 12 on dirt roads to the take out to drop a car. Then you drive back up the mountain to the Swamp Creek trailhead high on a ridge over the creek. Once all this is accomplished all that stands between you and Big Sands is a 2-3 mile hike on the Swamp Creek Trail, mostly downhill, and depending on conditions over lots of blown down trees.\n\nBig Sands is a big creek - don't expect a low volume scraper unless you go at low flows. The creek is placid at the trail's terminus, but quickly drops into a class IV rapid with an undercut wall and a 90 degree left turn at the bottom. At this point the gradient begins really dropping out. A notable 8-10 foot waterfall can be run early in the trip. Other than this drop, which begins and ends in a pool, Big Sands offers only long rapids with multiple drops and holes. At higher water the rapids are very stompy and offer little or no chance to stop once committed to a rapid - and did I mention the rapids are long, often disappearing around blind corners? In the middle of the steep stuff is a mandatory portage called pancake which is a 10+foot drop that lands on rock, and is followed by a stout class V multi-drop rapid. There are alot of rapids on Big Sands. They are high quality and often stout. Wood is always a concern, and there are several seives that paddlers should be aware of.\n\nAfter negotiating all the rapids on Big Sands, paddlers still have about a mile of great Class IV whitewater on White Sands, followed by a mile or two of class II run-out.\n\nThe scenery in the Big Sands Canyon is truly stunning. Talus fields generally border the entire river and vertical granite walls tower over its entire length. Thankfully, portaging and scouting is relatively easy throughout the run if you are comfortable carrying a boat across talus fields. The river is in the Bitterroot Selway Wilderness and is certainly worthy of the designation. Hiking out would range from epic to impossible depending on your location.\n\nIdaho, the Whitewater State, G. Amaral (Watershed Books; 1990)","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"3.4","correlations":[],"pointOfInterestIDs":["109774","115026"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-114.5836264288903,46.390125796778754],[-114.58306973258448,46.3902293946598],[-114.58245933258542,46.3904849946594],[-114.5817117325866,46.3907863946589],[-114.58126153258729,46.39100379465856],[-114.58091059925448,46.39112212799171],[-114.58030779925544,46.39125559465822],[-114.5796365325898,46.39144632799122],[-114.57927019925705,46.39159132799102],[-114.57898033259079,46.39183919465728],[-114.57891173259094,46.39205672799028],[-114.57868279925793,46.392365727989784],[-114.57834713259177,46.392609794656096],[-114.57804193259227,46.3926135946561],[-114.57786639925922,46.39250299465624],[-114.57762993259291,46.39241912798974],[-114.5772789992601,46.392228394656684],[-114.57675253259424,46.392110127990186],[-114.57627193259503,46.39214059465684],[-114.57604299926203,46.39244579465634],[-114.57566913259598,46.3929187946556],[-114.57540213259637,46.393025594655455],[-114.5746697325975,46.3931667946552],[-114.57444079926455,46.39330412798836],[-114.574120399